 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5965+) **Python 2.4 Docker compile GitHub workflow:** added [`python24-compile.yml`](/.github/workflows/python24-compile.yml), which runs `Assets/Python` and `PrivateMaps` through real CPython 2.4 syntax/bytecode compilation using our separate [`wonderingabout/python-2.4-docker`](https://github.com/wonderingabout/python-2.4-docker) GHCR image. This complements Ruff by checking the old parser Civ4 embeds, without launching Civ4 or importing engine-only modules. A deliberate [test confirmed it fails](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27897204427) on Python 2.5+ ternary syntax such as `SAS_MAGIC_PY24_COMPILE_BREAK_TEST = 1 if True else 0` in `SASMagicNumbers.py`. See [`.github/workflows/README.md`](/.github/workflows/README.md#python-24-compile-workflow), and [README.md (Python Scripts)](/README.md#python-scripts) for screenshots.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5962+) **Light source archive helper:** added [`make_light_source_zip.py`](/LLM_Helpers/README.md#make_light_source_zippy), which creates a timestamped no-compression AdvCiv-SAS source/data/docs archive under `LLM_Helpers/outputs` or a chosen output folder. This avoids repeatedly manually selecting and tediously creating an updated ZIP of each file/folder each time, of the same useful core files/folders ChatGPT or other LLMs can read or needs, while leaving unneeded or too heavy to use ones (e.g., as of now no .fpk, .tga, .dll, or pycache folders, art assets folder), when sharing compact mod context with local tools or LLMs.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5931+) **Dependabot for GitHub Actions:** added Dependabot tracking for GitHub Actions versions to help address Node.js runtime deprecation warnings such as `actions/<hidden-email>` and `actions/<hidden-email>` still using Node.js 20 (see [<hidden-email>#24](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/pull/24)). This should reduce manual maintenance and make future action-version updates easier to notice and apply. See [`.github/workflows/README.md` current build checks](/.github/workflows/README.md#current-build-checks).
-- **Handicap XML comparison helper:** added [`compare_handicap_infos.py`](/LLM_Helpers/compare_handicap_infos.py), a report-only, mod-agnostic helper that compares two explicit `CIV4HandicapInfo.xml` file paths, inside or outside this mod folder, by handicap index; shows missing fields as blanks, includes absolute/percentage numeric deltas, and embeds a spreadsheet-friendly TSV matrix. The shipped stable example [`handicap_infos_compared.md`](/LLM_Helpers/examples/handicap_infos_compared.md) compares base AdvCiv 1.12 vs AdvCiv-SAS. See [LLM_Helpers (README.md)](/LLM_Helpers/README.md).
+- **Handicap XML comparison helper:** added [`compare_handicap_infos.py`](/LLM_Helpers/compare_handicap_infos.py), a report-only, mod-agnostic helper that compares two explicit `CIV4HandicapInfo.xml` file paths, inside or outside this mod folder, by handicap index; shows missing fields as blanks, includes absolute/percentage numeric deltas, and embeds a spreadsheet-friendly TSV matrix.
 - **Merged** the **old split/interdependent Foreign Advisor** implementation from the two-file setup (`CvForeignAdvisor.py` + `CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py`) into a **single unified** [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py) with the **full tab set** (as of now Relations/Glance/Active/Bonus/Info/Tech/Cities). In our findings, **this was the only screen file** using that **interdependent split** pattern, so merging it into one file directly **fixes that inconsistency** and **reduces maintenance burden**; other major screen files such as [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py) and [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py) are lengthy but unified files. By contrast, true alternatives use independent variants (for example BUG/non-BUG [CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py) / [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py) paths), not interdependent split files.
 - **Remove screen-dependent geometry computation** from `__init__` in advisors because this advisor object is created before a reliable screen context exists; doing layout in `interfaceScreen` **ensures correct values for the current resolution**. Keeping **only screen-independent edge constants** in `__init__` ensures **no redundant recomputation** is made again in `interfaceScreen`, and **catches loud screen-dependent errors** in `__init__`.
 - **Heavily refactor and simplify Sevopedia Main** so it is much easier to add, reorder, or modify or otherwise maintain categories. See [Sevopedia reworks (example 0.0)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-00-heavily-refactored-sevopedia-maintain-so-it-is-much-easier-to-maintain-or-customize).
@@ -432,7 +432,7 @@ Make some of the data-dense advisors use using a **higher constrast background t
 - **Main Interface (City Screen)**: Enhanced with a new **Great Person +n ICON** information in relevant Buildings' rows; added a new **Specialists Breakdown** and **Culture Breakdown**; added **optional extra rows** in the **Production Chooser Bar** (with optional separate blue ribbon, bar Y position and bar height position fine-tuning tunables (e.g., helps remove needless scroll bar when there are not more than max rows, or keep display symmetric or prettier)) and **optionally hide the unit bar** (`"PlotListPanel"`) (note: does not affect the production chooser outside of the city screen); added **Buttons** (i.e. icons) in the **Production Queue**; fixed some hard anchored items that now **dynamically** adjust to sides' width. **Beautified** it as well: removed the 3 gray bars ("Trade Routes", "Buildings", "Specialists"), increased sides' width, made bonuses columns even in width, and other changes. These changes allow to now display more information and reduce the need for scrolling or hovering. Also **enlarged** the **Bottom-Left** and **Bottom-Right** panels so they align dynamically with the enlarged **Side Panels**. Enhanced the **city bar** and **other bars**, e.g., `Lakamha: 16 - 12372 (4500BC)` or `Growing - 30/43 (4 Turns)`. Adjust **city camera** to the north (tunable) so extra rows can be shown without overflowing into bottom BFC plots in `CvGame::onCityScreenChange`. And other changes. See also [KI#101](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#101---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-gp-bar-tooltip-in-city-screen-not-showing-gp-from-obsolete-buildings-yet-seemingly-counting-them-for-the-total-gp-calculation).
 - **Main Interface (City Screen - Widgets/Clickable Buttons)**: Add **redirect to Sevopedia on click** (preserving `WIDGET_HELP` hover) for **Religion** and **Corporation** icons. Add a tunable **city bonus panel render mode**: **mode 0** keeps the old AdvCiv-SAS text glyphs (Civ4's `screen.setLabelAt`: smaller; also used as overflow fallback), **mode 1** uses base AdvCiv-style framed image buttons (Civ4's `setImageButton`) but now with **larger icons** when there is room, and **mode 2** uses frameless DDS rendering (Civ4's `addDDS`) with the same larger-size logic for a cleaner look. Active non-obsolete **Bonus** icons can open Sevopedia too (mode 0 text glyphs did not redirect to Sevopedia in testing; mode 1: left/right click; mode 2: right click only in our Python-only attempts so far). Split the **Draft group** into hurry controls on the right (and a **new draft button**) and config options on the right. Add building list filtering buttons ("Show All Buildings", "Show Regular Buildings Only", "Show National Wonders Only", "Show World Wonders Only") and restored **Production Chooser Bar** row-jump buttons with clearer hover text ("Scroll to Units/Buildings/Wonders"). Reduce **food/production top bars' size** so text does not overflow when upscaled (also helps preserve overall distance to side panels due to increasing base font size from body to label). Add **commerce sliders fast increment buttons** (`++ and --` optional buttons ("Min/Max Buttons in BUG Menu")) in city screen (matching the ones in map view) (not added in Finance Tab or Espionage Tab because these still have access to commerce sliders as of now at their right in map view). Change in [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py).
 - **Main Interface (Map View)**: **Reordered buttons** (end turn, city change arrows) and wrapped them in a **pretty panel**. Added buttons to unit stack, selected unit. Added **help text box** (`DefaultHelpArea`) (on the left side) optional **width adjustment** (negative value shrinks it). Make **x and y positions** (resolution-scaled), and **width** (hard pixel; not resolution-scaled) of the **unit bar** (`PlotListPanel`) **adjustable**, and **fix horizontal overflow of unit bar into scoreboard** when unit bar is full and scoreboard is hovered on (or toggle lock scoreboard hover is ON) (see [KI#124](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#124---fixed-likely-base-advciv-issue-map-view-unit-bar-overflows-into-hoveredexpanded-scoreboard)). Make **left-click on GP bar** open the **corresponding city's city screen**. Added a **Toggle show map annotations** (Alt + S **captions**, Alt + X **BFC marks**) button (next to the other buttons **above the Minimap**); the toggled state **persists on save and load**; reorganized buttons as part of this change (this takes the Event Log's former HUD icon former (it gets another one instead)). To accommodate this new minimap button's width, **reduce minimap buttons horizontal interspacing** so **last minimap button doesn't collide horizontally with globe view** button (except for squarish maps like as of now `BTG_Cross.py`, where this is a fine trade-off, and still improved significantly with this adjustment). See [README.md (Map annotations)](/README.md#map-annotations) and [KI#135](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#135---fixed-likely-base-advciv-issue-turn-status-text-collided-with-the-diplomacy-screen). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5941+) Optionally show **Plot coordinates on hover** (e.g., `63,46`) in hover help text. This makes it to discuss screenshots, review, or compare directly with BBAI logs and DLL diagnostics.
-- **Main Interface ((Map View) Scoreboard)**: do **not draw beyond** bottom of commerce sliders (previously it would overflow beyond top of the screen), add **+** (up, fast up) and **-** (down, fast down) **scroll buttons** (e.g., 1 by 1, 5 by 5) to choose **first and last leader shown** when the **number of leaders is high** (e.g., if there are 48 leaders to display and the scoreboard can only show ~30 leaders max). Note: the Info screen's score tab allows to see all leaders so this is a fine trade-off to avoid vertical overflow. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5968+) Add a **Center scoreboard scroll on the active player** button, and a **Toggle autocenter scoreboard scroll on the active player** button (default as of optionally now ON; manual scroll disables it). Add a **Toggle lock scoreboard hover button** so scoreboard is always hovered on even without hover (e.g., to see power ratios without having to hover), with an **optional default value** (as of now ON, to avoid always tediously clicking it the first time). Note: in first turns of the game the lock button effectively has no effect since power ratios are not yet visible. Add a **Toggle Background Style button** (AdvCiv **default at each save load/new game kept**; tunable) (e.g., blue panel, black50, empty (transparent)). Change in [Scoreboard.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/Scoreboard.py) and [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). See [README.md (Scoreboard)](/README.md#scoreboard).
+- **Main Interface ((Map View) Scoreboard)**: do **not draw beyond** bottom of commerce sliders (previously it would overflow beyond top of the screen), add **+** (up, fast up) and **-** (down, fast down) **scroll buttons** (e.g., 1 by 1, 5 by 5) to choose **first and last leader shown** when the **number of leaders is high** (e.g., if there are 48 leaders to display and the scoreboard can only show ~30 leaders max). Note: the Info screen's score tab allows to see all leaders so this is a fine trade-off to avoid vertical overflow. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5968+) Add a **Center scoreboard scroll on the active player** button, and a **Toggle autocenter scoreboard scroll on the active player** button (so that it auto does it without having to tediously redo it regularly; note: if the scroll up/down buttons are clicked, it disables autocenter to apply manual scrolling (can be reenabled by reclicking the toggle autocenter button again)) (default state at Civ4 launch as of now optionally ON). Add a **Toggle lock scoreboard hover button** so scoreboard is always hovered on even without hover (e.g., to see power ratios without having to hover), with an **optional default value** (as of now ON, to avoid always tediously clicking it the first time). Note: in first turns of the game the lock button effectively has no effect since power ratios are not yet visible. Add a **Toggle Background Style button** (AdvCiv **default at each save load/new game kept**; tunable) (e.g., blue panel, black50, empty (transparent)). Change in [Scoreboard.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/Scoreboard.py) and [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). See [README.md (Scoreboard)](/README.md#scoreboard).
 - **Main Interface (civilization flag):** **Removed the civilization flag** from the production buttons bar (next to minimap) to show more buttons instead and have a more efficient display. Instead, added **optional compact top-left civilization flag** (with same preserved BtS hover/click behavior) (if **enabled**, left **top text spacing is shifted to make room for the compact flag**). Unlike base AdvCiv, this **optional flag** is **also visible in city screen** because it does not interfere with bottom city-action buttons. This flag is useful to know player civ, hover for player traits, and click to capital's city screen. Default disabled (tunable) as it can be distracting and undesired.
 - **Worker recommendation highlights disabled**: turned off tile coloring for "worker-recommended plot to improve" (in `CvGame::updateColoredPlots` within `CvGameInterface.cpp`). Reasons: (1) avoids extra computation in both debug ([see for related info this autoplay info](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/Modding_Ressources/README.md#how-to-autoplay-let-the-ai-play-for-you-super-fast-gameplay--testing-tool-in-map-loaded-save-file-new-game-etc-view)) and normal play; (2) our worker logic now relies on `CvUnitAI::AI_bestCityBuild`, so the vanilla highlight often disagrees and can mislead; (3) the highlight was easily confused with **city site** recommendations. City-site suggestions remain enabled and intentionally prominent; in practice, they frequently pick **strong** locations—quite often as good as, or better than, typical manual choices. See [Settlers (AI)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md#settlers-ai). *Note:* the **displayed recommended settle city plots** don’t always match what the AI would settle if it were playing your civ in autoplay; the UI hint path may be (not sure) using a different logic from the reworked/optimized `AIFoundValue::evaluate`. Treat them as general information, not guarantees.
 
